  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115766",
      "title": "The afterRender and afterNextRender Lifecycle Functions",
      "lectureOrder": 137,
      "videoOrder": 130,
      "sourceHash": "587f7a09dcd8c4e90c057c69327b3153cf91e8448cd0582cf0c27b93c47cc483",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.6,
          "end": 3.69,
          "en": "Now, two other interesting lifecycle hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.69,
          "end": 6.69,
          "en": "that are actually registered differently",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.69,
          "end": 10.26,
          "en": "than the ngOoInit and all those other hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.26,
          "end": 14.343,
          "en": "are the afterNextRender and afterRender hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.45,
          "end": 20.37,
          "en": "These are also not available in older versions of Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.37,
          "end": 24.3,
          "en": "They have been added with Angular 16.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 24.3,
          "end": 28.143,
          "en": "And you do register them with help of the constructor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 29.82,
          "end": 32.76,
          "en": "So not as methods in the component class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 32.76,
          "end": 35.64,
          "en": "but instead with help of the constructor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 35.64,
          "end": 39.723,
          "en": "Because in that constructor you can then call afterRender,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 40.62,
          "end": 43.23,
          "en": "so this afterRender function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 43.23,
          "end": 46.57,
          "en": "which is imported from at Angular core",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 49.8,
          "end": 52.473,
          "en": "or alternatively, afterNextRender,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 54.18,
          "end": 57.01,
          "en": "which is also imported from at Angular core",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 58.92,
          "end": 60.63,
          "en": "and to both functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 60.63,
          "end": 63.393,
          "en": "you then pass a function as an argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 64.95,
          "end": 68.23,
          "en": "And here, our console log afterRender",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 69.63,
          "end": 72.767,
          "en": "and all console log afterNextRender.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 75.36,
          "end": 78.513,
          "en": "Now what's the idea behind these lifecycle hooks here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 79.8,
          "end": 81.682,
          "en": "Well, if you save that and you go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 81.682,
          "end": 82.77,
          "en": "and you reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 82.77,
          "end": 87.393,
          "en": "you see afterRender and afterNextRender are executed here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 88.8,
          "end": 91.146,
          "en": "But you'll also notice that afterRender",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 91.146,
          "end": 93.81,
          "en": "then is executed again and again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 93.81,
          "end": 97.083,
          "en": "basically whenever anything changes on that website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 98.37,
          "end": 101.43,
          "en": "So not if something changes in this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 101.43,
          "end": 102.9,
          "en": "this control component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 102.9,
          "end": 105.63,
          "en": "but anything anywhere on this website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 105.63,
          "end": 107.723,
          "en": "anywhere in this Angular app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 107.723,
          "end": 110.4,
          "en": "AfterRender is locked over and over again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 110.4,
          "end": 112.44,
          "en": "whenever any change occurs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 112.44,
          "end": 116.88,
          "en": "whereas, afterNextRender is not locked again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 116.88,
          "end": 119.7,
          "en": "Because the idea behind these hooks here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 119.7,
          "end": 122.7,
          "en": "is that they allow you to define functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 122.7,
          "end": 124.44,
          "en": "that should be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 124.44,
          "end": 127.11,
          "en": "whenever anything changes anywhere",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 127.11,
          "end": 129.87,
          "en": "in the entire Angular application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 129.87,
          "end": 132.72,
          "en": "or after the next change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 132.72,
          "end": 135.873,
          "en": "anywhere in the entire Angular application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 136.98,
          "end": 139.44,
          "en": "So it's always the entire application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 139.44,
          "end": 140.943,
          "en": "we're talking about here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 141.78,
          "end": 146.04,
          "en": "whereas the other lifecycle hooks like ngOoInit ends on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 146.04,
          "end": 148.743,
          "en": "refer to the component to which they belong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 150.06,
          "end": 152.235,
          "en": "With afterRender and afterNextRender,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 152.235,
          "end": 155.49,
          "en": "it's the entire application instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 155.49,
          "end": 156.81,
          "en": "But the difference then is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 156.81,
          "end": 159.09,
          "en": "that afterRender will execute a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.09,
          "end": 162.21,
          "en": "because it listens to all future changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 162.21,
          "end": 164.925,
          "en": "whereas afterNextRender will only be triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 164.925,
          "end": 169.82999999999998,
          "en": "for the next change anywhere in the entire application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 169.82999999999998,
          "end": 174.66,
          "en": "And therefore, if you have some code that should be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 174.66,
          "end": 177.09,
          "en": "whenever anything changes anywhere",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 177.09,
          "end": 181.08,
          "en": "or afterNext change anywhere in your application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 181.08,
          "end": 183.48,
          "en": "these two special hooks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 183.48,
          "end": 186.903,
          "en": "these special functions can be helpful.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
